WEBVTT

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:48.850
I know where to find your valley, Tsukasa.

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:51.440
I'm going to use it as a point of entry
to your peak.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.440
BACK DOOR

00:01:55.610 --> 00:01:58.240
Tsukasa, the CEO has arrived.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.990
Long time no see, sir.

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:04.580
A long time indeed, Tsukasa.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.750
How's your pet coming along?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:10.290
Very well, I am glad to say.
He is ready for a job.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:15.010
Before that, how would you like
to do a job with Hayashi's pet?

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:17.590
Really? May I?

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:22.180
I want you to grasp the big picture
of the department you work in,

00:02:22.350 --> 00:02:26.350
so that you can move into
a leadership role.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:29.900
You look pleased.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:34.440
I, erm... It's been a long time
since I saw Mr. Hayashi.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.190
It's only his pet you'll be meeting.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:41.620
Oh, I see...

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:43.370
Tsukasa,

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:46.580
do you know why this breed
of hunting dog

00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:48.620
is called a "pointer"?

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:54.040
I heard it's because it points out
the location of the game.

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:55.130
Exactly.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:58.470
And once it starts pointing,
it waits there just like that

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.840
until the hunter gives it an order.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:03.430
It's a pitiful animal.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:07.520
Even if its master forgets all about it,
it keeps waiting patiently.

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.150
Staying in the same pose forever
until it dies.

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.020
That's how obedient you should teach
your pet to be.

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:20.740
Or else it'll end up running off
just like Hayashi did.

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.370
Hayashi's not coming back, you know.

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:28.580
Let today be the last day
you look up to that traitor.

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.040
Mr. Hayashi...

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:33.080
Forever...

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.250
Forever...

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.210
Forever...

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:41.260
A pitiful dog waiting for its master...

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:43.930
Just like me.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.680
Are you really intending to change
my memories, Mr. Hayashi?

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.980
I'm sorry, Tsukasa.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.060
There's no other way, not anymore.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.690
I will carry the weight of your pain.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:02.820
Whatever it takes, I'm taking you with me.
Please understand.

00:04:09.450 --> 00:04:13.250
I see you're creeping in like a draft,
Mr. Hayashi.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:16.080
It'll take you a long time to get in
through the dog's eye.

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:19.340
The strength of my lock
isn't just for show, you know.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:22.420
Even so, I applaud you.

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:26.470
Always one step ahead,
you've made it all the way to my peak.

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:28.890
I certainly can't match your speed.

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:32.140
It's frustrating how slow I am.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:36.190
It must be down to my image being water...

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:39.110
Or so I had always mistakenly believed.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:43.990
But the water in a waterfall
flows at great speed.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:47.120
Why then, can I not travel that fast?

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.750
My pet certainly doesn't have
that problem, Mr. Hayashi.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:57.000
His image is a goldfish,
and he swims faster and faster.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.340
Do you know why?
It's because his lock is weak.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:06.760
A weaker lock means he has fewer limits
on his sensitivity and his speed.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:11.010
It wasn't because of my image.
It was my lock.

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.600
I made my lock so strong
that it restrains my movements.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:20.230
But you know what? There is somewhere
that my lock has no effect.

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.320
It's here, Mr. Hayashi.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:27.740
Here, in my peak, I have no limits.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:31.740
Indeed, the same is true
for all those with our abilities.

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:35.830
Standing atop your peak
makes you truly the king of the hill.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:40.750
Until, that is, an intruder appears.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.760
Because your peak is also a fragile place,
where your sensitivity is unchecked.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:49.140
So perhaps it is wise to have
a secure lock after all.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:55.140
I feel like I've caught a burglar who
was too focused on trying to pick my lock.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:00.400
By the way, Mr. Hayashi, I assume
you're familiar with puddles...

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:10.450
Yeah, you're right...

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:14.660
I guess it's not an easy question
to answer straight away.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:18.330
That's probably why they only told me
to sound you out.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:20.830
Looks like I messed up again...

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:22.380
Again?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.050
My cousin is always saying

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:29.130
that I only understand
things superficially.

00:06:29.510 --> 00:06:31.800
He says I'm soft in the head.

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.430
He's so rude. Always criticizing!

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:40.810
However hard I try at work,
he still treats me like a little kid!

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.060
Now she's just... whining?

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:48.700
He's six years older than me,
so he's known me since I was in diapers.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:51.570
-How old are you now?
-Who, me?

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:55.080
Oh, sorry! I shouldn't have asked.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:06:56.790
I'm 24.

00:06:57.870 --> 00:06:59.830
What's wrong? Do I look older?

00:07:00.290 --> 00:07:03.590
No! I mean, that's about what I thought.

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.420
Oops, it's time for me to leave.

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:11.590
Too bad we can't have that pizza.
I'll have them take it to your room later.

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.850
Oh, thanks.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.560
So she's five years older than me...

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.600
-I envy you, Satoru.
-Huh?

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:23.440
I wish I could use an image.

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.230
If I was able to go anywhere like that,

00:07:26.940 --> 00:07:29.110
I know exactly where I'd go.

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.360
Inside the memory of someone
who knew my mom.

00:07:33.570 --> 00:07:37.290
She died just after I was born,
so I don't have any memories of her.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.540
What's the earliest you can remember?

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.120
When I was five or so.

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:43.170
That's pretty early!

00:07:43.380 --> 00:07:46.380
Mr. Hayashi said he doesn't remember
anything from before he was 15.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:51.010
It's because my grandfather
took care of me since I was a baby.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:55.350
Of course... But then
 her grandfather was murdered.

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:59.270
And I wasn't like you. I've always been
able to make my own memories.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.520
Oh, right.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:05.400
If you can make memories on your own,
you don't need an image.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:08.150
Why not? They seem so useful!

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.950
I mean, they're just a last resort.

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.320
People like me who couldn't
create our own memories,

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:20.410
we had no choice but to use an image
to receive someone else's peak.

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:23.870
Not being able to form memories
 on your own is horrible.

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.170
It's like you're trapped inside people's
feelings and they're squashing you flat.

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:34.260
It's thanks to my image that I was able to
change and become like I am now.

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:38.560
You're better off having always been able
to make your own memories.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:40.600
I see...

00:08:42.100 --> 00:08:45.060
But someday, if I get chance,

00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:49.070
I'll take you inside the memory
of a person who knew your mom.

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.320
You'd do that?

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:54.280
The place where your mom is
at her most beautiful

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:56.530
is probably inside your dad's memory.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.950
We can't go there,
because my dad's not around either.

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:04.660
I think the best person would be the CEO.

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:08.380
He was my mom's brother
and was really fond of her.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.000
But, you know...

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:13.840
There's no way the CEO would
let someone inside his memory.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.680
Yeah, I guess most people
wouldn't like that.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:22.100
Um... how long are you staying here?

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:24.770
For a while yet, I think.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:28.310
You never know,
we might even work together.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.730
Yeah?

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:34.150
Okay, sleep well.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.450
Ah, good ni...

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.280
Working with her...

00:09:40.660 --> 00:09:44.580
Sounds more fun than working
 with Mr. Katsuragi, that's for sure.

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:47.370
Where is this?!

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:52.300
Have you forgotten
how your own peak looks?

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.470
That's the rainbow
from your peak, is it not?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.590
But how did you...?

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:00.390
A little trick of mine. A back door.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:03.520
Since I am water, I can make puddles.

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.390
So whenever I enter a memory locus,

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.150
I'm able to leave a puddle behind
as an image.

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:13.900
I entered your peak when you
shared it with me.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:18.780
Since I've been there, of course
I know where it is.

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:23.580
But that doesn't necessarily mean
I can find the way in,

00:10:24.290 --> 00:10:26.660
because peaks are hidden by valleys.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:29.960
So I used the puddle I left in your memory

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:33.920
to link your peak with mine,
then I synced my way here.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:37.720
It's a trick that's only possible
when my lock is unbolted.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:39.760
Tsukasa...

00:10:40.430 --> 00:10:43.680
I really didn't think it would work
as well as this.

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:47.600
Do you have any idea what you're doing?!

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:50.350
Your lock is supposed
to keep your sensitivity in check.

00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.400
But you're using it in reverse!

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:57.400
You removed the lock from your peak
to come here,

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:00.280
so it's linked directly to your peak!

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:04.580
If you crush this place, your peak
will be affected as well!

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:09.540
And what does that matter anymore?

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.000
Tsukasa...

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.710
No...

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:25.600
My goal was always to be like you.

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:30.600
What are you doing, Tsukasa?
Get out of here now!

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.230
Stop this, Tsukasa!
You'll be crushed too!

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:40.150
Why...

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:43.240
are you worrying about me?

00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:47.790
Shit.

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.370
Shit!

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.880
Why the hell has this happened?

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:03.090
So...? How much did Satoru know?

00:12:03.510 --> 00:12:06.390
It seems Hayashi hadn't said
anything to him.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:10.100
He was surprised when I told
him the story.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:13.900
He did seem to know about
most of Hayashi's past, though.

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:17.020
He must've done some calculations
when I told him my age

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.980
and guessed that I was
a member of the family,

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:22.990
because he wasn't shocked
to hear I was the CEO's niece.

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.740
You idiot!

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:27.280
That means he knows
all about what happened!

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:30.910
He knows that the qigong masters were
all killed by the CEO.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:34.920
That's why he guessed you must be
part of the family if you're still alive!

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.790
Oh... right.

00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.050
This is why I say you're soft in the head!

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:45.550
Somebody who thinks the qigong masters are
alive would guess you were one of them!

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:49.180
So they'd sure as hell be surprised
to find out you're a relative!

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:52.180
-You don't need to shout at me.
-Shut up, you moron!

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.600
Do you even realize I was babysitting
you on the monitor

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:57.980
because I thought he might
alter your memories?

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:01.820
Who knows what else Hayashi might have
put into his head!

00:13:02.070 --> 00:13:06.280
We don't have any idea what Hayashi's
been doing for the last two years!

00:13:07.490 --> 00:13:09.370
In any case...

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:12.370
I need to separate these two.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:14.160
Shit!

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.960
-Um...
-Hey!

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:20.590
I told you to wait in the damn car.
All lookouts are to withdraw!

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.260
Get the hell out of here
before somebody sees you!

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:24.420
Yes, sir!

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:28.260
He said we need to leave right now.

00:13:29.010 --> 00:13:30.560
Was the long-haired dude there?

00:13:30.760 --> 00:13:32.220
Yeah, he was there.

00:13:32.430 --> 00:13:35.230
No way! How did he get out?

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.600
We had the front and back
of the building covered.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:42.150
Something's definitely up. Mr. Katsuragi
was asleep in the cigarette store too...

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:46.360
Maybe he was drugged or something?

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:49.820
The long-haired dude
looked wasted just now...

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:51.240
Hey...

00:13:51.780 --> 00:13:53.750
You guys ever heard of "crushers"?

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:55.580
They're some kind of kung fu...

00:13:55.750 --> 00:13:58.120
-Shh! You'd better not say any more.
-Huh?

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:01.880
Start spreading rumors
and you'll get labeled a spy.

00:14:02.130 --> 00:14:05.630
So you'd better keep your mouth shut
if you want to keep breathing.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:09.300
Dammit! Is this what you were on about?

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:11.890
If something happens to me,

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:14.600
make sure you take me to Hiroki.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:16.390
What do you mean "something"?

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:19.770
I promised Hiroki I'd be back.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.770
He trusts me and will be waiting for me.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:25.490
So no matter what happens,

00:14:25.780 --> 00:14:27.650
I have to go back to him.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:32.490
What else? Come on, you can do this...

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.790
Of course, Hayashi!

00:14:35.040 --> 00:14:37.660
I need to do something about him as well.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:43.840
H...Hello. This is Katsuragi.
Hayashi has been crushed.

00:14:44.130 --> 00:14:45.800
I think Tsukasa...

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:50.970
No. I found Tsukasa crushed as well,
lying next to Hayashi.

00:14:52.550 --> 00:14:55.560
I'm taking him back to the goldfish store.

00:14:55.720 --> 00:14:57.730
I'll leave Hayashi up to you.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:15:01.770
Come quick! Tsukasa has been crushed!

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:03.650
For real?

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:05.940
Seems he was crushed along with Hayashi.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:08.320
You're serious?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:10.360
What's funny?

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:15.450
Earlier today that arrogant jerk
was talking back to me.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.580
He thinks he's high and mighty
just because he uses an image.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:23.080
It's images that have enabled our family
to climb as high as we have!

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:26.300
Without them we wouldn't be able
to create "babies" either!

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:28.630
If both Hayashi and Tsukasa are gone,

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.840
who on earth is going to
create "babies" for us now?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:34.970
What're you talking about, Jin?

00:15:35.600 --> 00:15:38.850
There are still two pets left.

00:15:39.560 --> 00:15:43.600
Whichever is more of a good boy,
 we'll get to create "babies" for us.

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.360
Dammit.

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:48.690
Why hasn't he replied to my messages?

00:15:49.070 --> 00:15:53.820
Tsukasa, if you don't come back soon,
our store is gonna go under.

00:15:55.660 --> 00:15:58.870
Is it really a good idea
to take him there like this?

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.500
What if Hiroki freaks out?

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:03.040
Shit!

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:07.380
There's no way I'd be able
to bring him under control.

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:10.010
I'd better call for some reinforcements.

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.300
Dammit! Where'd I put my damn phone.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:17.890
What the hell?

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:21.270
Why am I carrying this around with me?

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:24.900
It's supposed to be in a safe place!

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:28.770
Let's store all our secrets
 in this little box.

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:31.030
I know...

00:16:31.690 --> 00:16:34.910
I'll give it to Mr. Matasa
for safekeeping.

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:36.660
It'll be okay.

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:41.410
Mr. Matasa will take it somewhere safe.

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:47.170
It's Tsukasa! He's back!

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.550
I've just arrived.

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:54.180
Yes, I'll leave him here.

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:56.890
Control yourself, Hiroki.

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:58.550
Tsukasa...?

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:11.730
Damn you, Katsuragi!
What did you make him do?

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:14.820
It wasn't me! He went off by himself!

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:16.200
Katsuragi!

00:17:16.490 --> 00:17:20.080
Don't! This is your fault anyway
for shirking your responsibilities.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:21.540
What?

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:25.000
It was supposed to be you and Tsukasa
doing this job.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:28.830
It's because he had to do it himself
that he's ended up like this.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:30.920
This is my fault?

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:33.710
Damn right! So blame yourself, not me!

00:17:34.260 --> 00:17:38.680
I didn't say you had to. I'll do
 the Company's jobs by myself.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:43.640
All I've done is carry out his last wish
by bringing him all the way here.

00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.230
A thank you wouldn't go amiss!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:48.400
His last wish? But why...?

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:49.860
Damned if I know!

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.900
Whatever the reason,

00:17:52.280 --> 00:17:54.690
he's crushed now and that's that.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:57.530
So just give up on him, Hiroki.

00:17:57.740 --> 00:17:58.700
No...

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:02.370
He's not crushed.

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.250
Looks pretty damn crushed to me...

00:18:04.410 --> 00:18:06.870
Shut up! Just leave already, Katsuragi!

00:18:07.790 --> 00:18:10.710
Fine. I'm going. Ungrateful little...

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.630
Tsukasa! Tsukasa! Wake up!

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:17.930
Don't leave me! Wake up!

00:18:18.130 --> 00:18:20.510
Dammit! Tsukasa!

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.060
What's this?

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:27.480
Are the tanks leaking?

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:30.150
No, that's not it.

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:32.440
How weird...

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:33.900
Where's it coming from?

00:18:40.070 --> 00:18:42.910
Tsukasa, is it your water?

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:47.250
Whatever's happened to your memory loci,
your image is still working.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.290
You're still in there somewhere.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:52.460
Hold on. I'll find you, Tsukasa!

00:18:55.630 --> 00:18:58.550
Shit! What's happened to Tsukasa's peak?

00:19:03.550 --> 00:19:07.220
Why's there all this blood
in that beautiful river?

00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:11.810
Where are you, Tsukasa?

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:17.570
How am I supposed to find him
in this place!

00:19:19.070 --> 00:19:21.160
It's no good. I keep sinking...

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:24.700
Wait, that's it.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.450
It might be full of blood,
but it's still water.

00:19:29.210 --> 00:19:31.790
And it must be flowing from somewhere.

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:35.340
Over there!

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:38.590
Shit.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:40.840
Dammit!

00:19:45.430 --> 00:19:46.220
Tsukasa!

00:19:47.720 --> 00:19:48.680
Tsukasa.

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:52.310
Tsukasa! Hey!

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:57.360
Tsukasa...

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:00.740
What are you doing, Hiroki?

00:20:01.240 --> 00:20:04.490
I came to save you,
because I saw your water.

00:20:05.160 --> 00:20:07.580
-Water...?
-Come on, you have to get up.

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.960
Of course...
It's because your lock is weak.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.420
No! Don't sink!

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:18.130
Why are you worrying about me?

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:19.630
Tsukasa?

00:20:20.670 --> 00:20:23.510
I think this is my first time
in a car with you, Mr. Hayashi.

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:28.260
No, Tsukasa! If we don't do something,
you'll be crushed for real!

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.650
Hiroki...

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:46.200
Tsukasa! You're back to normal!

00:20:46.490 --> 00:20:47.450
Where are we?

00:20:47.660 --> 00:20:49.830
Don't worry. We're in my peak.

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:52.500
This is your peak?
The one I gave you?

00:20:53.330 --> 00:20:55.790
It's the river that was in your peak.

00:20:56.000 --> 00:21:00.130
Since I'm a fish, I figured
I only needed the river.

00:21:00.750 --> 00:21:02.380
Why have you brought me
into your peak?

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:06.640
What do you mean why?
You were about to be crushed!

00:21:06.890 --> 00:21:08.890
Your peak is all messed up!

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:13.100
So I thought I'd wash the bad stuff away
with the water from my peak.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:15.980
I've gotta push the valleys
out of your peak.

00:21:16.350 --> 00:21:19.520
You mean go back to my peak,
with the link to here still in place?

00:21:20.070 --> 00:21:24.780
I can do it, right? Because this peak
came from you in the first place.

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:28.910
It's my back door trick in reverse...

00:21:30.080 --> 00:21:33.080
Yeah, you can do it.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:35.790
Let's get going then.

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:39.630
I'm gonna make your river beautiful again!

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:03.360
Your tail... It's all torn up...

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:10.740
Thanks, Hiroki.

00:22:15.450 --> 00:22:18.120
Welcome back, Tsukasa.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:55.010
Artist: Akiko Monden
